  "answer_text": "I have successfully measured a 3x3 grid of Raman spectra at the requested coordinates (X = 40.0, 40.1, 40.2 mm; Y = 27.0, 27.1, 27.2 mm).\n\n### Experiment Report\n**1. Objective**\nThe goal was to map the strongest Raman peak position and intensity across a specific 3x3 grid of coordinates to assess spatial uniformity of the sample's spectral response.\n\n**2. Measurement Conditions**\n- **Laser Power:** 20% (selected based on biological sample safety guidelines from the knowledge base).\n- **Exposure Time:** 1.0 s per acquisition.\n- **Acquisition Mode:** Accumulate (requested 5 accumulations to improve SNR).\n- **Focus:** An autofocus procedure was performed at the center of the grid (40.1, 27.1), settling at Z = -0.0224 mm, which was then maintained for all points.\n\n**3. Summary of Results**\nA total of 9 spectra were acquired. The strongest peak in every single spectrum occurred at approximately **508.7 cm⁻¹**. The intensities varied slightly across the grid, with the highest intensity observed at (40.1, 27.2) and the lowest at (40.2, 27.2).\n\n**4. Spectral Analysis**\n- **Peak Position:** Constant at $\\sim$508.7 cm⁻¹.\n- **Intensity Range:** ~449 to 575 counts.\n- **Observations:** The uniformity of the peak position suggests a homogeneous material across the measured area. No saturation was observed as intensities remained well within the detector's linear range.\n\n**5. Conclusion**\nThe sample exhibits highly consistent spectral characteristics across the 3x3 grid, with a dominant feature at 508.7 cm⁻¹. The spatial variation in intensity is minimal, indicating a relatively uniform surface or concentration of the Raman-active species.\n\n```json\n{\"peak_positions\": [508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743, 508.702743]}\n```",
